      "scene_no": 6,
      "template_id": "concept_diagram",
      "teacher_script": "Several vital accessory organs assist in digestion without directly touching the food. The liver produces bile, the gallbladder stores it, and the pancreas secretes powerful enzymes and hormones, all working in concert to break down fats, proteins, and carbohydrates.",
